e Writing", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/20/2026", "sessionEndDt": "05/16/2026", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Many things get done and decisions get made in organizations through acts of persuasion and social influence. In lieu of formal power, people must be able to persuade others to come around to their point of view. At the same time, employees frequently influence one another and the broader organizational culture without even trying through social influence processes such as conformity, compliance, and behavioral contagion. In this course, students will learn about established and emerging research on persuasion and social influence by reading academic journal articles and then translating these articles into op-ed style essays that are understandable to the broader public, applicable to current events, and accurately represent the research findings.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Priority given to: ILR sophomores.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2024SP, 2023SP, 2015FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 371056, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "3260", "titleShort": "Building Power from Nothing", "titleLong": "Building Power from Nothing", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "AWI-IL", "descr": "IL-Advanced Writing Intensive", "descrformal": "IL-Advanced Writing Intensive Elective", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{"attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "crseAttrValues": "(AWI-IL, ICE-IL)"}], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9282, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:55PM", "timeEnd": "04:10PM", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/05/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "bb686", "firstName": "Brittany", "middleName": "M.", "lastName": "Bond"}], "pattern": "MW", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/16/2026", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/20/2026", "sessionEndDt": "05/16/2026", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This is a course about power and influence. We will discuss how to map power and interest patterns in organizations, how to understand various groups' interests and objectives, and how to operate effectively in organizational environments. Organizational actors differ in the power and resources that they bring to bear in order to advance their perspectives. Students will learn how to advance personal interests, even from positions of little structural advantage. This class will develop frameworks as well as a range of practical tools to address these goals. The course will take a macro approach to studying power and influence, focusing on organizational culture, politics, influence, and leadership. Students will learn how to build power from nothing, as well as how to become successful agents of lasting organizational change.We will draw from a wide range of material drawn from the business and public sector. Class preparation will range from watching classic movies to reading magazine articles to prepping case studies.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Priority given to: ILR juniors and seniors.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "ILRID 1535.", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2024SP, 2022FA, 2022SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 374277, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "4640", "titleShort": "Business Strategy", "titleLong": "Business Strategy", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{"attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "crseAttrValues": "(ICE-IL)"}], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9334, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "10:10AM", "timeEnd": "11:25AM", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/05/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "fsb42", "firstName": "Forrest", "middleName": "S", "lastName": "Briscoe"}], "pattern": "MW", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/16/2026", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/20/2026", "sessionEndDt": "05/16/2026", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "002", "classNbr": 9335, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:40AM", "timeEnd": "12:55PM", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/05/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "fsb42", "firstName": "Forrest", "middleName": "S", "lastName": "Briscoe"}], "pattern": "MW", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/16/2026", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/20/2026", "sessionEndDt": "05/16/2026", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "The ability to create and evaluate business strategies is a critical skill for leaders in organizations of all types. This course introduces concepts and tools to help students develop an understanding of how strategies are formed and managed, and how competitive advantage may be created and sustained. We discuss different business models, the importance of customers, how to assess an organization's resources and capabilities, and how to adapt to changes in the competitive environment. Creating a business strategy is a fun, interactive process; the class is designed to mirror this by using real-world case studies, supplemented by a mix of in-class activities and interactive lectures. The course concludes with a series of case competitions, including a final competition judged by a panel of external experts.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Enrollment limited to: juniors and seniors.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "HADM 4410, ILROB 4640", "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2025SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 370731, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "4795", "titleShort": "Managerial Negotiations", "titleLong": "Managerial Negotiations", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "crseAttrValueGroups": [{"attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "crseAttrValues": "(ICE-IL)"}], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9272, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:30AM", "timeEnd": "11:00AM", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/05/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "al2488", "firstName": "Alice", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Lee"}], "pattern": "R", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/16/2026", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "ICE-IL", "descr": "IL-In-College Advanced Electiv", "descrformal": "IL-In-College Advanced Electives", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRD", "gradingBasisShort": "Graded", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/20/2026", "sessionEndDt": "05/16/2026", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course aims to help students improve their skills in two fundamental ways. One is knowledge-oriented: students learn frameworks and concepts for analyzing conflict. Students acquire terms and models for identifying the type of conflict that exists in a situation and the potential costs and benefits of different strategies and tactics. Based on this, students should be able to interpret situations, plan tactics, and recognize and react to their counterpart's behavior. A second and complementary route to improving as a negotiator is practice-oriented: students complement their analytical tools with behavioral skills. Negotiation and conflict ultimately come down to behaviors-how a manager opens a potentially volatile conversation, how a mediator uncovers information, how a negotiator frames an offer or a concession. Practicing these behaviors, and understanding how other parties perceive and react to them, is essential to improving as a negotiator. The course provides continuing opportunities for hands-on practice and also provides feedback, discussion, and occasions for reflection.                   Through role-play exercises, lecture, reading, and discussion, the course begins with basic dynamics in negotiation and adds complexity in stages, including multiple issues, multiple parties, mediation, agents, and coalitions. Some exercises involve numerical analyses, others revolve around qualitative conflicts. By the end of the course, students should be able to comfortably and confidently approach most any conflict or negotiation: analyzing its nature, understanding their own objectives, and plotting an approach that will give them the best shot at achieving their goals.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Enrollment limited to: juniors and seniors.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2023SP, 2022SP, 2021SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 371057, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "5260", "titleShort": "Being Effective: Power & Influ", "titleLong": "Being Effective: Power and Influence", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9283, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:25PM", "timeEnd": "02:40PM", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/05/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "bb686", "firstName": "Brittany", "middleName": "M.", "lastName": "Bond"}], "pattern": "MW", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/16/2026", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/20/2026", "sessionEndDt": "05/16/2026", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "All organizations are fundamentally political. People have different self-interests, perspectives, and objectives. Players also differ in the power or resources that they bring to bear to advance their perspectives. If you are to be effective, both with respect to the goals of an organization and with respect to your personal goals, you need to be able to map these differences, understand various groups' interests and objectives, and understand how to operate in an organizational environment. In addition to being able to think strategically, you also need a set of skills that can be summarized via the words \"power, persuasion, and influence.\" This more sociological course will expand students' ability to successfully navigate the social and cultural organizational landscapes to be effective agents of change.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Enrollment limited to: graduate students.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "IL", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2024SP, 2022FA, 2022SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 362602, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILROB", "catalogNbr": "5790", "titleShort": "Managerial Negotiations", "titleLong": "Managerial Negotiations", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9207, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:15AM", "timeEnd": "01:45PM", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/05/2026", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "al2488", "firstName": "Alice", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Lee"}], "pattern": "R", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Enrollment priority given to: Master of Industrial and Labor Relations (MILR) students."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/20/2026", "endDt": "05/16/2026", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionM